From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 10:58:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Load Carla's library from lib/carla on Windows

Carla installs libcarla_native-plugin in lib/carla, and carlabase links
to it. Elsewhere the RPATH from carla-native-plugin.pc finds it there;
Windows has no RPATH and searches neither lib/carla nor the plugin's
own directory, so carlabase, and with it Carla Rack and Patchbay, fail
to load. Load the library by its full path before the plugins: loading
carlabase then finds it in the process, as the discovery loop already
relies on for ZynAddSubFxCore. Without Carla installed nothing loads,
and the two instruments are left out as before.

Upstream: not submitted
---
 src/core/PluginFactory.cpp | 7 +++++++
 src/lmmsconfig.h.in        | 1 +
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/PluginFactory.cpp b/src/core/PluginFactory.cpp
index 936b33c..bc7c76d 100644
--- a/src/core/PluginFactory.cpp
+++ b/src/core/PluginFactory.cpp
@@ -77,6 +77,13 @@ PluginFactory::PluginFactory()
 
 	QDir::addSearchPath("plugins", ConfigManager::inst()->workingDir() + "plugins");
 
+#if defined(LMMS_BUILD_WIN32) && defined(LMMS_HAVE_CARLA) && !defined(LMMS_PORTABLE_LAYOUT)
+	// carlabase links to libcarla_native-plugin, which Carla keeps in
+	// lib/carla. Windows does not search there, so load it by its path.
+	QLibrary(QDir::cleanPath(qApp->applicationDirPath()
+		+ "/../lib/carla/libcarla_native-plugin.dll")).load();
+#endif
+
 	discoverPlugins();
 }
 
diff --git a/src/lmmsconfig.h.in b/src/lmmsconfig.h.in
index 921ba1e..1f1c83b 100644
--- a/src/lmmsconfig.h.in
+++ b/src/lmmsconfig.h.in
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #cmakedefine LMMS_HOST_X86_64
 
 #cmakedefine LMMS_HAVE_ALSA
+#cmakedefine LMMS_HAVE_CARLA
 #cmakedefine LMMS_HAVE_FLUIDSYNTH
 #cmakedefine LMMS_HAVE_JACK
 #cmakedefine LMMS_HAVE_WEAKJACK
